Obligatory I-solved-nethack post follows:

Well, I finally solved nethack after over four months of playing.
I played a priest with a final AC of -45 and a total of 74 HPs.
I knew it was going to be a good game when I found a +3 cloak of
protection, speed boots, and a magic lamp in a shop on level four.
There were two shops, four bones levels, and several altars.

Good stuff:  blessed +4 gray dragon scale mail 
             blessed +4 helm of brilliance
             blessed +6 cloak of protection
             +6 speed boots
             blessed +5 Stormbringer

I found a magic marker which I blessed and recharged along with many
useless scrolls that I made into enchant armor/weapon.  I didn't see
a single scroll of genocide during the entire game.

Scariest moment:  When I went to apply my stethoscope to Medusa, but 
accidentally removed my blindfold instead.  It was during one of my
"extra" turns so I was able to blind myself again in time.

Biggest annoyance: The WoW in the castle was cursed and started out with
only one wish.

Funniest message:  Some monster (I think it was a marilith) said something
about ripping out my lungs.

I knew I was going to win when I left hell and didn't see the Wiz again
until dlvl 2.

Biggest abuse:  Using a pick-axe to rob shops and resell stuff for gold.
No bag of holding, infinite gold, or polypiling.

Morals: Low armor class is better than high hit points.  Holy water is
very useful.

